    --  COMMUNITY STATS WIDGET  Ã¢â‚¬â€  LayoutOrder 3 (between perf and server)
    --
    --  Border: faithful port of nazuro.lol's conic-gradient spinning border.
    --
    --  How the web version works (verbatim from their CSS):
    --    @property --angle { syntax:'<angle>'; initial-value:0deg }
    --    @keyframes spin-border { to { --angle: 360deg } }
    --    ::before {
    --      background: conic-gradient(from var(--angle),
    --        transparent 92%, #ff8c1e 96%, #fff 98%, #ff8c1e 100%);
    --      animation: spin-border 2s linear infinite;
    --      mask: content-box exclude, border-box;  Ã¢â€ Â punches hole so only border shows
    --    }
    --
    --  Roblox port:
    --    Ã¢â‚¬Â¢ Outer wrapper Frame (1px inset on each side) with UIStroke thickness 2
    --      and UICorner radius 8 Ã¢â‚¬â€ this IS the border ring.
    --    Ã¢â‚¬Â¢ A child Frame fills the wrapper, BackgroundTransparency=1, with a
    --      UIGradient whose Rotation spins on Heartbeat.
    --    Ã¢â‚¬Â¢ The UIGradient ColorSequence replicates the conic stops:
    --        0%   transparent  (92% of 360Ã‚Â° = 331Ã‚Â° of dark)
    --        92%  orange       (4Ã‚Â° ramp up)
    --        96%  white        (2Ã‚Â° hot peak)
    --        98%  orange       (2Ã‚Â° ramp down)
    --        100% transparent  (loop back)
    --      The UIStroke Color is set to this gradient's color at the rotation
    --      angle Ã¢â‚¬â€ but Roblox UIStroke doesn't support gradients directly.
    --      Workaround: 8 thin Frame "ring slices" sized to cover each edge,
    --      each with its own UIGradient rotated to match its edge orientation,
    --      all driven by one shared rotation variable. This gives smooth color
    --      across all four sides simultaneously.
    --    Ã¢â‚¬Â¢ Outer ambient glow Frame pulses orange behind the card.
    --    Ã¢â‚¬Â¢ On exec tick: glow slams bright, counter pops with Back easing.
    -- Ã¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢ÂÃ¢â€¢Â

